# Notification config for scheduled/headless runs (docs/proactive-operations.md §8).
# Copy this to telegram_config.txt (gitignored, never committed) and fill in real
# values. Used both by the in-session agent (to notify when a plan is ready) and
# by the wrapper scripts' own failure-alert path (works even if the agent never
# got to run at all).
#
# Real values needed — not yet supplied as of this file's creation:
#   TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN — either a new dedicated bot for this system, or the
#     existing Petty Cash bot's token reused with a different chat/channel.
#     Your call; either works mechanically.
#   TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID   — the chat/channel id to send notifications to.
#
# TELEGRAM_APPROVAL_REAL_EXECUTION (added 2026-08-21, see docs/proactive-
#   operations.md §8a and docs/architecture.md §3 guardrail 1's open-question
#   note) — code-level kill switch for scripts/telegram_approval_listener.py.
#   Leave unset/false until Suraj has explicitly decided whether a verified
#   Telegram button tap counts as direct approval for guardrail 1's purposes.
#   While unset/false, APPROVE taps are recorded and reported but no claude
#   session is dispatched and no Meta/Instagram call is made. Set to "true"
#   only after that decision is made — no redeploy needed, re-read fresh on
#   every tap.

TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
TELEGRAM_APPROVAL_REAL_EXECUTION=false
